---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Fourier lab" description="Draw any closed shape and watch it decomposed into a Fourier series, then redrawn by a chain of rotating circles. Interactive, no libraries." imageAlt="Fourier lab: draw a shape, get its Fourier series">
  <section class="block lab">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive · Fourier series · epicycles</p>
    <h1>Draw anything. Get its Fourier series.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Draw a closed shape below. The path is sampled, treated as a sequence of complex numbers, and run through a
      discrete Fourier transform. Every term becomes one rotating circle. Chain the circles tip to tail and they redraw
      your shape. Start with a few circles and add more: the grey line is your drawing, the red line is what the
      circles can manage.
    </p>

    <div class="stage">
      <canvas id="lab" aria-label="Drawing canvas: draw a closed shape with your mouse or finger"></canvas>
      <div class="hint" id="hint">Draw here</div>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <label>Circles <span id="terms-out">5</span>
        <input type="range" id="terms" min="0" max="100" value="27" />
      </label>
      <div class="quick" role="group" aria-label="Quick circle counts">
        <button type="button" data-n="1">1</button><button type="button" data-n="2">2</button><button type="button" data-n="3">3</button><button type="button" data-n="5">5</button><button type="button" data-n="10">10</button><button type="button" data-n="20">20</button><button type="button" data-n="50">50</button><button type="button" data-n="100">100</button><button type="button" data-n="all">all</button>
      </div>
      <label>Speed <span id="speed-out">1×</span>
        <input type="range" id="speed" min="0.25" max="4" step="0.25" value="1" />
      </label>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="show-circles" checked /> show circles</label>
      <div class="presets">
        <span class="hud-label">Presets</span>
        <button type="button" data-preset="heart">Heart</button>
        <button type="button" data-preset="star">Star</button>
        <button type="button" data-preset="square">Square</button>
        <button type="button" data-preset="infinity">Infinity</button>
        <button type="button" data-preset="reactor">Reactor</button>
        <button type="button" id="clear" class="danger">Clear</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="readout">
      <div class="formula-box">
        <p class="hud-label">The series</p>
        <p class="eq">f(t) = Σ<sub>k</sub> c<sub>k</sub> · e<sup>ikt</sup>, with c<sub>k</sub> = (1/N) Σ<sub>n</sub> z<sub>n</sub> · e<sup>−ikn·2π/N</sup></p>
        <p class="meta" id="meta">Draw a shape to compute its coefficients.</p>
        <p class="meta" id="fit"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="terms-box">
        <p class="hud-label">Largest terms</p>
        <table id="terms-table" aria-live="polite">
          <thead><tr><th>k</th><th>|c<sub>k</sub>|</th><th>phase</th><th>role</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="explainer">
      <h2>What is happening</h2>
      <p>
        A closed drawing is a periodic function: walk the path once and you are back where you started. Treat every
        sample point as a complex number <code>z = x + iy</code>. The discrete Fourier transform then asks, for each
        integer frequency <code>k</code>, how much of the path is "a circle of radius <code>|c<sub>k</sub>|</code>
        turning <code>k</code> times per lap, starting at angle <code>arg(c<sub>k</sub>)</code>". Negative
        <code>k</code> turns the other way. Add all the circles together, tip to tail, and the last tip retraces the
        drawing exactly. Drop the small ones and you get a smooth approximation, which is the whole idea behind
        compression, filtering, and why a square wave needs infinitely many odd harmonics.
      </p>
      <p>
        Why do the circles vanish so fast? For a smooth drawing the amplitudes fall off roughly as
        <code>1/k²</code>, so by the twentieth term the circle is smaller than a pixel. Draw something with sharp
        corners and the fall-off slows to <code>1/k</code>: corners are expensive. That is the same reason a square
        wave's ringing never quite goes away.
      </p>
      <p>
        The hero on the home page is the one-dimensional version of this: five odd harmonics with amplitudes
        <code>4/(πn)</code> summing towards a square wave.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lab h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .lab .lede { margin-top: 0; }
  .stage { position: relative; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--bg-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .stage canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: min(70vh, 560px); touch-action: none; cursor: crosshair; }
  .stage .hint { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center; pointer-events: none; font-family: var(--hud); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--text-dim); opacity: 0.7; transition: opacity 0.3s; }
  .stage .hint.off { opacity: 0; }
  .controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.2rem 2rem; align-items: end; margin: 1.2rem 0 1.6rem; }
  .controls label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; font-family: var(--hud); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .controls label span { color: var(--accent); margin-left: 0.4rem; }
  .controls input[type="range"] { width: 200px; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .controls .check { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .controls .check input { accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .quick { display: flex; gap: 0.3rem; align-items: center; }
  .quick button { all: unset; cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .quick button:hover, .quick button.on { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
  .presets { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .presets .hud-label { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--gold); margin-right: 0.3rem; }
  .presets button { all: unset; cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--hud); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.74rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; color: var(--text); transition: all 0.15s; }
  .presets button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
  .presets button.danger:hover { border-color: var(--gold); color: var(--gold); }
  .readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; gap: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .readout > div { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--bg-2); padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem; }
  .readout .hud-label { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--gold); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .eq { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--head); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .eq sub, .eq sup { font-size: 0.7em; }
  .readout .meta { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .readout .meta b { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500; }
  #terms-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  #terms-table th { text-align: left; font-family: var(--hud); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-dim); padding: 0 0.4rem 0.4rem 0; }
  #terms-table td { padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem 0.2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--text); }
  #terms-table td.k { color: var(--accent); }
  #terms-table td.role { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .explainer h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .explainer p { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 720px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .readout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>

<script>
  type Cx = { re: number; im: number };
  type Term = { k: number; re: number; im: number; amp: number; phase: number };

  const canvas = document.getElementById('lab') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!;
  const hint = document.getElementById('hint')!;
  const termsIn = document.getElementById('terms') as HTMLInputElement;
  const termsOut = document.getElementById('terms-out')!;
  const speedIn = document.getElementById('speed') as HTMLInputElement;
  const speedOut = document.getElementById('speed-out')!;
  const showCircles = document.getElementById('show-circles') as HTMLInputElement;
  const meta = document.getElementById('meta')!;
  const fit = document.getElementById('fit')!;
  const tbody = document.querySelector('#terms-table tbody')!;
  const quick = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.quick button')];
  const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  const SAMPLES = 400;
  let w = 0, h = 0, dpr = 1;
  let drawing = false;
  let raw: Cx[] = [];          // points while drawing (centre-relative css px)
  let path: Cx[] = [];         // resampled closed path
  let coeffs: Term[] = [];     // sorted by amplitude
  let trace: Cx[] = [];
  let t = 0, raf = 0;

  let ACC = '255, 74, 74', GOLD = '242, 182, 50', TEXT = '226, 217, 211';
  const readTheme = () => {
    const s = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    ACC = s.getPropertyValue('--accent-rgb').trim() || ACC;
    GOLD = s.getPropertyValue('--gold-rgb').trim() || GOLD;
    TEXT = s.getPropertyValue('color-scheme').trim() === 'light' ? '44, 35, 32' : '226, 217, 211';
  };

  // The slider runs 0..100 and maps logarithmically onto 1..N, so the low
  // counts where the fit is visibly rough get real travel.
  let exactN: number | null = null; // set by the quick buttons, cleared by the slider
  const termsInUse = () => {
    const N = Math.max(1, coeffs.length);
    if (exactN !== null) return Math.max(1, Math.min(N, exactN));
    const v = Number(termsIn.value) / 100;
    return Math.max(1, Math.min(N, Math.round(Math.exp(Math.log(N) * v))));
  };
  const sliderFor = (n: number) => {
    const N = Math.max(2, coeffs.length);
    return Math.round((Math.log(Math.max(1, n)) / Math.log(N)) * 100);
  };

  function resize() {
    dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
    w = canvas.clientWidth; h = canvas.clientHeight;
    canvas.width = w * dpr; canvas.height = h * dpr;
    ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
  }

  // Resample a polyline to n points evenly spaced by arc length, closing the loop.
  function resample(pts: Cx[], n: number): Cx[] {
    const closed = [...pts, pts[0]];
    const seg: number[] = [];
    let total = 0;
    for (let i = 1; i < closed.length; i++) { const d = Math.hypot(closed[i].re - closed[i - 1].re, closed[i].im - closed[i - 1].im); seg.push(d); total += d; }
    if (total === 0) return pts.slice(0, 1);
    const out: Cx[] = [];
    let i = 0, acc = 0;
    for (let s = 0; s < n; s++) {
      const target = (s / n) * total;
      while (i < seg.length - 1 && acc + seg[i] < target) { acc += seg[i]; i++; }
      const f = seg[i] === 0 ? 0 : (target - acc) / seg[i];
      out.push({ re: closed[i].re + (closed[i + 1].re - closed[i].re) * f, im: closed[i].im + (closed[i + 1].im - closed[i].im) * f });
    }
    return out;
  }

  function dft(z: Cx[]): Term[] {
    const N = z.length, out: Term[] = [];
    for (let k = -Math.floor(N / 2); k < Math.ceil(N / 2); k++) {
      let re = 0, im = 0;
      for (let n = 0; n < N; n++) {
        const a = (-2 * Math.PI * k * n) / N, c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a);
        re += z[n].re * c - z[n].im * s;
        im += z[n].re * s + z[n].im * c;
      }
      re /= N; im /= N;
      out.push({ k, re, im, amp: Math.hypot(re, im), phase: Math.atan2(im, re) });
    }
    return out.sort((a, b) => b.amp - a.amp);
  }

  function role(k: number) {
    if (k === 0) return 'centre offset';
    if (Math.abs(k) === 1) return k > 0 ? 'main loop, anticlockwise' : 'main loop, clockwise';
    return `${Math.abs(k)}× per lap, ${k > 0 ? 'anticlockwise' : 'clockwise'}`;
  }

  // RMS distance between the n-term reconstruction and the sampled path.
  function fitError(n: number) {
    const N = path.length; let acc = 0;
    for (let m = 0; m < N; m++) {
      const tt = (2 * Math.PI * m) / N; let x = 0, y = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const c = coeffs[i]; const a = c.k * tt + c.phase; x += c.amp * Math.cos(a); y += c.amp * Math.sin(a); }
      acc += (x - path[m].re) ** 2 + (y - path[m].im) ** 2;
    }
    return Math.sqrt(acc / N);
  }

  function updateReadout() {
    if (!coeffs.length) return;
    const n = termsInUse();
    termsOut.textContent = String(n);
    const fmt = (x: number) => (Math.abs(x) >= 100 ? x.toFixed(0) : x.toFixed(1));
    const c0 = coeffs.find((c) => c.k === 0)!;
    const tiny = coeffs.slice(0, n).filter((c) => c.amp < 1).length;
    meta.innerHTML = `${path.length} samples · ${coeffs.length} coefficients · <b>${n} circle${n === 1 ? '' : 's'} in use</b>` +
      (tiny ? ` (${tiny} of them under 1 px, stacked at the tip)` : '') + ` · c₀ = (${fmt(c0.re)}, ${fmt(c0.im)})`;
    let minX = 1e9, maxX = -1e9, minY = 1e9, maxY = -1e9;
    path.forEach((p) => { minX = Math.min(minX, p.re); maxX = Math.max(maxX, p.re); minY = Math.min(minY, p.im); maxY = Math.max(maxY, p.im); });
    const size = Math.hypot(maxX - minX, maxY - minY) || 1;
    const err = fitError(n);
    fit.innerHTML = `fit error: <b>${err.toFixed(1)} px RMS</b> (${((err / size) * 100).toFixed(1)}% of the shape size). Add circles and watch it fall.`;
    quick.forEach((b) => b.classList.toggle('on', b.dataset.n === String(n) || (b.dataset.n === 'all' && n === coeffs.length)));
  }

  function commit(pts: Cx[]) {
    if (pts.length < 8) return;
    path = resample(pts, SAMPLES);
    coeffs = dft(path);
    trace = []; t = 0;
    exactN = Math.min(5, coeffs.length);
    termsIn.value = String(sliderFor(exactN));
    hint.classList.add('off');
    tbody.innerHTML = coeffs.slice(0, 8).map(c => `<tr><td class="k">${c.k}</td><td>${c.amp.toFixed(1)} px</td><td>${((c.phase * 180) / Math.PI).toFixed(0)}°</td><td class="role">${role(c.k)}</td></tr>`).join('');
    updateReadout();
    start();
  }

  function frame() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);
    const cx = w / 2, cy = h / 2;

    // the drawing itself, solid and dim, so the fit can be judged against it
    if (path.length) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${TEXT}, 0.35)`; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath(); path.forEach((p, i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(cx + p.re, cy + p.im) : ctx.moveTo(cx + p.re, cy + p.im))); ctx.closePath(); ctx.stroke();
    }
    // live stroke while drawing
    if (drawing && raw.length > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${GOLD}, 0.9)`; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath(); raw.forEach((p, i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(cx + p.re, cy + p.im) : ctx.moveTo(cx + p.re, cy + p.im))); ctx.stroke();
      return;
    }
    if (!coeffs.length) return;

    const n = termsInUse();
    let x = cx, y = cy;
    const circles = showCircles.checked;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const c = coeffs[i];
      const ang = c.k * t + c.phase;
      const nx = x + c.amp * Math.cos(ang), ny = y + c.amp * Math.sin(ang);
      if (circles) {
        // every circle in use is drawn, however small
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${GOLD}, ${c.amp < 1 ? 0.6 : 0.32})`; ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, Math.max(c.amp, 0.4), 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke();
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${GOLD}, 0.7)`;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, y); ctx.lineTo(nx, ny); ctx.stroke();
      }
      x = nx; y = ny;
    }
    trace.push({ re: x, im: y });
    if (trace.length > path.length) trace.shift();

    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ACC}, 0.1)`; ctx.lineWidth = 6;
    ctx.beginPath(); trace.forEach((p, i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(p.re, p.im) : ctx.moveTo(p.re, p.im))); ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ACC}, 0.95)`; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath(); trace.forEach((p, i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(p.re, p.im) : ctx.moveTo(p.re, p.im))); ctx.stroke();
    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${ACC}, 1)`; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();

    t += ((2 * Math.PI) / path.length) * Number(speedIn.value) * (reduce ? 0 : 1);
    if (t > 2 * Math.PI) t -= 2 * Math.PI;
  }

  function loop() { frame(); if (!document.hidden) raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop); }
  function start() { cancelAnimationFrame(raf); raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop); }

  // Drawing
  const pos = (e: PointerEvent): Cx => { const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(); return { re: e.clientX - r.left - w / 2, im: e.clientY - r.top - h / 2 }; };
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { drawing = true; raw = [pos(e)]; coeffs = []; trace = []; canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); hint.classList.add('off'); start(); });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (!drawing) return; const p = pos(e); const l = raw[raw.length - 1]; if (Math.hypot(p.re - l.re, p.im - l.im) > 1.5) raw.push(p); });
  const end = () => { if (!drawing) return; drawing = false; commit(raw); };
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', end);
  canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', end);
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerleave', end);

  // Presets
  const presets: Record<string, (s: number) => Cx[]> = {
    heart: (s) => Array.from({ length: 200 }, (_, i) => { const a = (i / 200) * Math.PI * 2; return { re: s * 16 * Math.sin(a) ** 3, im: -s * (13 * Math.cos(a) - 5 * Math.cos(2 * a) - 2 * Math.cos(3 * a) - Math.cos(4 * a)) }; }),
    star: (s) => Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => { const a = (i / 10) * Math.PI * 2 - Math.PI / 2, r = i % 2 ? s * 7 : s * 17; return { re: r * Math.cos(a), im: r * Math.sin(a) }; }),
    square: (s) => [{ re: -s * 14, im: -s * 14 }, { re: s * 14, im: -s * 14 }, { re: s * 14, im: s * 14 }, { re: -s * 14, im: s * 14 }],
    infinity: (s) => Array.from({ length: 200 }, (_, i) => { const a = (i / 200) * Math.PI * 2; const d = 1 + Math.sin(a) ** 2; return { re: (s * 20 * Math.cos(a)) / d, im: (s * 20 * Math.sin(a) * Math.cos(a)) / d }; }),
    reactor: (s) => { const out: Cx[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < 120; i++) { const a = (i / 120) * Math.PI * 2; out.push({ re: s * 16 * Math.cos(a), im: s * 16 * Math.sin(a) }); } for (let i = 0; i <= 3; i++) { const a = (i / 3) * Math.PI * 2 - Math.PI / 2; out.push({ re: s * 9 * Math.cos(a), im: s * 9 * Math.sin(a) }); } out.push({ re: s * 16, im: 0 }); return out; },
  };
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-preset]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => { const s = Math.min(w, h) / 44; commit(presets[b.dataset.preset!](s)); }));
  document.getElementById('clear')!.addEventListener('click', () => { raw = []; path = []; coeffs = []; trace = []; tbody.innerHTML = ''; meta.textContent = 'Draw a shape to compute its coefficients.'; fit.textContent = ''; quick.forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('on')); hint.classList.remove('off'); ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h); });

  termsIn.addEventListener('input', () => { exactN = null; trace = []; updateReadout(); });
  quick.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => { if (!coeffs.length) return; const n = b.dataset.n === 'all' ? coeffs.length : Number(b.dataset.n); exactN = n; termsIn.value = String(sliderFor(n)); trace = []; updateReadout(); }));
  speedIn.addEventListener('input', () => { speedOut.textContent = `${Number(speedIn.value).toFixed(2).replace(/\.?0+$/, '')}×`; });

  readTheme(); resize();
  window.addEventListener('resize', () => { resize(); trace = []; });
  window.addEventListener('themechange', readTheme);
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { if (!document.hidden) start(); });
  commit(presets.heart(Math.min(w, h) / 44));
</script>
